## Commands

```powershell
python scripts/refresh_zenodo.py
python scripts/build_artifacts.py
python scripts/verify.py
python scripts/zenodo_release.py preview --paper <stable-paper-id>
python scripts/zenodo_release.py sync-draft --paper <stable-paper-id> --token-file <path>
python scripts/zenodo_release.py verify-draft --paper <stable-paper-id> --token-file <path>
python scripts/zenodo_release.py publish --paper <stable-paper-id> --token-file <path>
```

Zenodo synchronization is successor-draft first. Publication remains an
explicit author decision after inspecting the generated PDF and metadata.
`sync-draft` replaces obsolete draft PDFs and verifies the uploaded checksum;
`verify-draft` requires exact reviewed title, version, description, and one PDF;
`publish` repeats that preflight before submission and records the resulting
public DOI, concept id, version, and URL in `catalog/publication-ledger.json`.
